      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MAJOR EXPRESS NZ (6) led and fought well to go under by just a head when resuming from a long layoff last week. Draws wider but has won three of four second-up attempts so should be improved and has yet to miss a place here. GOODTIME LOUIS (3) has been racing well and looks close to a win following back-to-back placings here. Led from wider and stuck on for third at his latest appearance, beaten 4 metres. Has the early speed to take advantage of the low so could break through. There was plenty of merit in the latest performance of CAPTAIN SAID SO (5) when he drew wider and worked but stuck on for a 1.6m second. ELITE FLEET (4) has been solid from tougher barriers since a close second here last month. Go well.",
